Pharmacy Invoice Discrepancy



Backend

It is built with Express (v5) + TypeScript.


Structure

backend/
├── build/                  
│   └── utils/               
│       ├── discrepancyChecker.js
│       └── index.js
├── node_modules/            
├── src/                    
│   ├── utils/             
│   │   └── discrepancyChecker.ts   mismatches
│   └── index.ts             
├── uploads/               
├── package.json            
├── package-lock.json
├── tsconfig.json     




Tech Stack

Runtime: Node.js
Language: TypeScript
Framework: Express 5
Middleware: cors → Enable cross-origin requests
            multer → Handle file uploads
Utilities: xlsx → Read/write Excel files
            axios → Make external HTTP requests


Setup Instructions

1. Install dependencies
 $ npm install

2. Development mode
Start the server with ts-node (auto-reloads when code changes):
 $ npm run dev
Runs src/index.ts.

3. Build and run (production)
Compile TypeScript → JavaScript, then run:
 $npm run build
 $npm run start
This runs the compiled build/index.js.



NPM Scripts

Script             Description
npm run dev        Start backend in development mode (ts-node)
npm run build      Compile TypeScript → JavaScript
npm run start      Run the compiled backend server


Configuration

Uploads are stored in /uploads.
Excel files are processed via SheetJS.
Discrepancy checking logic is implemented in src/utils/discrepancyChecker.ts.


API Endpoints              
Method              Endpoint             Description
GET                 /api/invoices        Fetch all invoices    
POST                /api/invoices        Create a new invoice
POST                /api/upload          Upload an Excel file (multer)
GET                 /api/export          Export invoices as Excel
GET                 /health              Health check (optional)


Utilities
src/utils/discrepancyChecker.ts

Provides logic for validating and comparing invoices
Useful for detecting mismatches between uploaded invoice files and existing records
Exported functions can be used by routes/controllers




Frontend


It is built with React + TypeScript and provides a user-friendly interface to:
Manage invoices
Upload Excel files
Export invoice data
Interact with the backend API


Project Structure

frontend/
├── public/                 
├── src/                   
│   ├── components/        
│   ├── pages/             
│   ├── hooks/             
│   ├── App.tsx            
│   └── index.tsx          
├── package.json
├── package-lock.json
├── tsconfig.json          


Tech Stack

React 19 + TypeScript
React Router v6 – Client-side routing
Axios – HTTP client for backend communication
SheetJS (xlsx) – Excel import/export support
Jest + React Testing Library – Unit testing



Installation & Setup

1. Install dependencies
 $ npm install

2. Development server
 $ npm start

3. Production build
 $ npm run build


NPM Scripts

Script              Description
npm start           Run development server (CRA)
npm run build       Build the frontend for production
npm test            Run tests using React Testing Library + Jest
npm run eject       Eject CRA config (not recommended)


API Integration

The frontend communicates with the backend via Axios.
 
Update the API base URL in code

Typical calls include:
Fetching invoices
Uploading Excel files
Exporting invoice data


